From 4714944839bb996e56902881f58718f14bf23d3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:25:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: GGML_ARIFI_Q8_0_CM1_2D=<roles> two-digit int8
 activations for Q8_0 MMQ (candidate B)

lane-296 night int8 maker R3 (HQ seat-68, 2026-09-29). Candidate B keeps the listed Q8_0 roles on the int8 coopmat1
MMQ but gives them ~15-bit activations: q1 = round(x/d1) as today, then q2 = round((x - q1*f16(d1))/d2) from a
residual variant of quantize_q8_1 (spec constant RESIDUAL). The MMQ runs once on q1 and once on q2 into two
split-k slices, summed by split_k_reduce (split_k forced to 1 on this path). Q8_0 weights are exact int8 and the
accumulation is exact int32, so the only error left is the second digit's rounding. Default (unset) = unchanged.
Role log prints INT8x2 for those roles.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Lane: lane-296
---
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-types.h      |  3 +
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp          | 78 ++++++++++++++++---
 .../vulkan-shaders/quantize_q8_1.comp         | 34 +++++++-
 3 files changed, 101 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

